WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
We're here with Eric Kim,

2
00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.690
author of his debut cookbook, "Korean American."

3
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.650
And Eric is bringing back the nostalgic TV dinner

4
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.090
with a modern twist.

5
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.420
I mean, I love this.

6
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.910
I talk about TV dinners all the time.

7
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.670
I feel like we need to modernize them.

8
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.860
What was your like point of view?

9
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.430 line:15%
You know, I really think that a TV dinner

10
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.900 line:15%
is about the comforting flavors

11
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.810 line:15%
that you remember from your childhood.

12
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.651
You know, this one's just a little more homemade,

13
00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:28.270
but the potatoes they get kind of like crispy at the edges.

14
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.326
Oh yeah, they do.

15
00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:30.291
That was really good.

16
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:32.970
And you do, you have like a little medley.

17
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.880
I love that those are also garnished,

18
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.440
which we didn't have on this one,

19
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.050
but we're gonna garnish right now.

20
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.153
Some sesame seeds.

21
00:00:39.153 --> 00:00:40.510
That's it.
With a little Sesame seed.

22
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.280
Good way to portion control too.

23
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.113
Yeah, it's true.

24
00:00:43.113 --> 00:00:46.288
We have two best friends in the audience, Whitney and Tim.

25
00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:47.300 line:15%
Where are you?

26
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.682 line:15%
Hi, guys.

27
00:00:48.682 --> 00:00:50.360 line:15%
(audience applauds)

28
00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.480 line:15%
Hi.

29
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.410 line:15%
And we like communal eating here.

30
00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.060 line:15%
So will you guys taste this along with us?

31
00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.570
Oh, absolutely.
Yes.

32
00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.470
How long have you guys been friends?

33
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:02.343
Three years.

34
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:04.980
Oh my God.
I'm so excited.

35
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.372
What'd she eat first?

36
00:01:06.372 --> 00:01:07.205
You like it?

37
00:01:07.205 --> 00:01:09.200
I'm so happy for you.

38
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.290
So happy to be new friends with you, Eric.

39
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.970
This is the most beautiful sauce.

40
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.400
It's so sweet and tangy.

41
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.410
And tangy and sweet and like savory.

42
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.650
Oh my God.

43
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.290
Worcestershire sauce is amazing if you like really use it.

44
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:29.600
I like overdoing flavors to balance each other out.

45
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.980
I also find potato sauce,

46
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.800
even though this is on the warmer side,

47
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.540
cooling to the palette after something so zesty.

48
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.373
Exactly.

49
00:01:37.373 --> 00:01:40.777
Whitney and Tim, thoughts quickly before we end the show.

50
00:01:40.777 --> 00:01:42.190
Amazing.
So good.

51
00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.160
Delicious.

52
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.290
The ribs are so good.

53
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.230
The sauce is just, ugh.

54
00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.520
It's incredible.

55
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.920
I'm so glad.
Very happy.

56
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.980
Oh my God, well, thank you so much for eating with us.

57
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:55.967
And Eric Kim, your beautiful new cookbook,

58
00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:58.690
"Korean American, Food That Tastes Like Home,"

59
00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:00.270
which really is about home.

60
00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.890
It's, you know, a love letter to your mother.

61
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.860
And I think this is a show about writing love letters

62
00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.500
in book forms to our families.

63
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.970
So thank you so much.

64
00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.080
This is sold wherever books are sold.

65
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.715
Get your hot little hands on this beautiful book.

66
00:02:14.715 --> 00:02:17.882 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

